      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Baseline data are presented of the ECAT Angina Pectoris Study. Both plasminogen activator inhibitor and fibrinogen were positively associated with a number of cardiovascular risk factors such as smoking, body mass index, and also with the presence of coronary stenosis. Results indicate a role of the hemostatic system in the progress of coronary arteriosclerosis."},
